 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the agriculture and markets law, in relation to the care of\nanimals",
    "basePrintNo": "S3828",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S3828-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §401, Ag & Mkts L",
    "lawSection": "Agriculture and Markets Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S3828\n\nSPONSOR: METZGER\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the agriculture and markets law, in\nrelation to the care of animals\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis legislation provides grooming, sanitation, and veterinary require-\nments for pet dealers.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1- Amends paragraphs (e), (g), and (h) of subdivision 1 of\nsection 401 of the agriculture and markets law. These amendments include\nrequiring facilities which house animals to include regular diurnal\nlight cycles of either natural or artificial light. Pregnant or nursing\ndogs must be provided with sufficient space to have freedom of movement\nand postural adjustments. Lastly, isolation areas for ill animals must\nalso meet the overall housing requirements for healthy animals.\n\nSection 2 -Amends subdivision 2 of section 401 of the agriculture and\nmarkets law, to include the requirement that primary enclosures for\nanimals be cleaned daily and sanitized weekly.\n\nSection 3 -Amends paragraph (c) of subdivision 3 of section 401 of the\nagriculture and markets law to include the requirement that food recep-\ntacles remain sanitary.\n\nSection 4 - Amends subparagraphs (iv) and (v) of paragraph (a) of subdi-\nvision 5 of section 401 of the agriculture and markets law which\nrequires annual veterinary examinations for all adult dogs or cats on a\npet dealer's premises. This provision applies to dealers who sell or\noffer to sell twenty-five or more dogs or cats per year to the public\nfor profit that are born and raised on the dealer's residential prem-\nises.\n\nSection 5 - Amends section 401 of the agriculture and markets law by\nadding a new subdivision 8 requiring pet dealers to engage in regular\ngrooming.\n\nSection 6 - Effective Date - 90th day.\n\n \nEXISTING LAW:\n\nUnder section 401 of the agriculture and markets law, there are many\nstandards of animal care.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation will provide additional standards of care for pet deal-\ners. Included within this legislation are requirements that nursing and\npregnant animals have sufficient space, grooming light, and sanitation\nstandards. Over the years, there have been reports of unscrupulous puppy\nmills mistreating animals. This legislation aims to ensure that all\nanimals under the care of a pet dealer meet new requirements of care.\n\nPet dealers must be held to standards that will promote the safety good\nhealth, and overall wellbeing of the animals in their care. This legis-\nlation will afford much needed protections to improve the quality of\nlife of these animals and will prevent negligent treatment by pet deal-\ners.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2017 - 2018 : S6784 / Advances to third reading / Passed Assembly\n2015 - 2016: S7800 / Referred to Agriculture / Passed Assembly\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\n90th Day\n",
